Supply Chain Resilience
A risk assessment indicator for each inbound shipment
The problem to solve
Socio economic unrest (port strikes)
Political upheaval (like the Bangladesh student unrest)
Financial issues with suppliers
Meteorological issues like cyclones etc are all reported on different channels, in different geographies and in different languages.
Understand these and flag a risk to a shipment if the geography from which it is being sources is at risk or the path the shipment is taking on land, or ocean is at risk.

Last Mile Network Planning
Given a geo-location, assess which polygon it should belong to; Additionally, how to define polygons given a set of OD pairs
The problem to solve
Imagine a quick commerce retailer. Assessing where to have an inventory fulfillment centre/dark-store and how to define a polygon which it can fulfill orders to. That is the problem which can save upto 20% of last mile delivery cost.

Baggage Operations & Airport Efficiency
Predictive transfer bag rescue
The problem to solve
For every connecting bag, continuously evaluate whether it is likely to miss its onward flight by combining bag scans, incoming-flight delay, connection time, airport/belt conditions, gate changes and interline hand-offs. Instead of discovering a missing bag at destination, identify a bag while intervention is still possible and recommend whether to expedite, reroute, reflight or otherwise intervene

Travel Disruption Intelligence
A disruption risk score for each scheduled flight, route and hub for the next 24-72 hrs
The problem to solve
Meteorological issues (storms, fog, cyclones, volcanic ash)
Air traffic control and labour strikes (union notices in French, German, Italian etc.)
Geopolitical airspace closures and conflict (NOTAMs, government advisories, local news)
Airport congestion and staffing shortages.
These are all reported on different channels, in different formats and in different languages. Understand these and flag a risk to a flight if its origin, destination or route is at risk, estimate the cost (extra fuel, rebooking, hotel vouchers, passenger compensation) and recommend the cheapest mitigation (reroute, extra fuel, aircraft swap, proactive rebooking)

Hotel Revenue & Inventory Optimization
Cancellation Risk & Inventory Recapture Engine
The problem to solve
Identify which live reservations are likely to cancel and, importantly, when they are likely to cancel by combining channel, booking lead time, rate plan, deposit/payment status, booking modifications, guest history, market demand, events and other relevant signals.

Use the resulting risk to support decisions such as inventory reopening, deposit requests, wait-list activation or controlled overbooking within defined limits

Travel Payment Fraud & Chargebacks
A fraud risk score at checkout, plus a dispute-likelihood score for each completed booking after a disruption
The problem to solve
Stolen card / card-not-present fraud
Account takeover and loyalty points fraud
Friendly fraud and refund abuse
Disruption-triggered disputes (delays, cancellations, hotel overbooking).
Signals are spread across payment gateways, booking systems, loyalty platforms, flight status feeds and customer communications.

Flag risky bookings without blocking genuine travellers, predict which bookings will be disputed after a disruption, trigger a proactive refund, voucher or rebooking before the customer goes to their bank, and auto-assemble evidence to fight invalid disputes

